---
import { SITE } from "../data/site";
import Doc from "../layouts/Doc.astro";
---

<Doc
	title="Privacy policy"
	description="Paperwren's privacy policy. The app collects nothing, has no analytics or ads, and never connects to the internet. Here is what stays on your device and how to clear it."
	label="Privacy policy"
	heading="Paperwren collects <em>nothing.</em>"
	path="/privacy/"
	updated="27 September 2026"
>
	<p class="lead">
		Paperwren is a document viewer. This policy is short because Paperwren
		collects almost nothing, and what it keeps never leaves your device.
	</p>

	<h2>What Paperwren collects</h2>
	<p>
		Nothing. Paperwren does not collect, transmit, sell or share any personal
		data. It has no analytics, no advertising, no trackers and no crash
		reporting, and it does not connect to the internet.
	</p>

	<h2>What stays on your device</h2>
	<h3>Recent files</h3>
	<p>
		The names and locations of documents you open, their size and where you
		stopped reading, so the app can list them and resume. You can turn this
		off, limit it, or clear it in Settings.
	</p>
	<h3>Private copies of files</h3>
	<p>
		On Android, when you open a file from the picker or from another app,
		Paperwren keeps a private copy that only it can read, so the file still
		opens from your recents after you close the app. Each file is stored once,
		copies are capped at 250 MB in total (oldest removed first), and you can
		delete them all in Settings.
	</p>
	<h3>Your settings</h3>
	<p>Choices like your theme and how PDFs open.</p>
	<h3>PDF passwords</h3>
	<p>
		Used in memory to open that file, then forgotten. They are never written
		anywhere.
	</p>

	<h2>Permissions</h2>
	<p>
		The Android app requests no permissions at all, including internet access.
		It only sees the files you open with it or share to it. Android's cloud
		backup is turned off for Paperwren, so its data does not travel with your
		backups either.
	</p>

	<h2>Files you open</h2>
	<p>
		Documents are read and displayed on your device only. Paperwren never
		uploads them, because it never talks to any server.
	</p>

	<h2>Deleting your data</h2>
	<p>
		Clear recents and private copies in Settings, or uninstall the app, which
		removes everything it stored. There is no account, so there is nothing to
		delete anywhere else.
	</p>

	<h2>Children</h2>
	<p>Paperwren collects no data from anyone, including children.</p>

	<h2>This website</h2>
	<p>
		This site sets no cookies, runs no analytics and serves its own fonts and
		scripts. Your browser talks only to the host serving these pages, which may
		keep standard server logs.
	</p>

	<h2>Changes</h2>
	<p>
		If a future version ever changes any of this, this page will be updated and
		the app will tell you before the change takes effect.
	</p>

	<h2>Contact</h2>
	<p>
		Questions go to the project's <a class="link" href={SITE.issues} rel="noopener">issue tracker</a>.
	</p>
</Doc>

